      "content": "When onion cells are damaged, the ruptured cytoplasm mixes the enzyme **alliinase** with the amino acid substrate **S-alk(en)yl-L-cysteine sulfloxide**. Alliinase catalyzes the rapid decarboxylation and oxidation of the substrate to generate the unstable intermediate **1-propenyl sulfenic acid**, which immediately reacts with the enzyme itself to form the stable final product, syn-propanethiol-S-oxide. This sequence demonstrates how physical trauma triggers a precise chemical cascade, allowing you to explain cell biology alongside the formation of that specific choking compound.",
